%description:
Tests adaptiveDelayedAcks=true, the quickack mode of Linux. The first data
segment gives the server a quickack budget (tcp_incr_quickack(): half the
window in full-sized segments, here 8), so it acknowledges the 100 bytes of
t=1.0 and of t=1.6 at once. Without the parameter, each ACK waits for the
delayed ACK timer (200 ms).

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

*.cli_app.sendScript="1.0 100; 1.6 100"
*.srv_tcp.adaptiveDelayedAcks = true

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[1.001 A003] A.1000 > B.2000: A 1:101(100) ack 501 win 16384 
[1.003 B002] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 101 win 16384 
[1.601 A004] A.1000 > B.2000: A 101:201(100) ack 501 win 16384 
[1.603 B003] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 201 win 16384 
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
sending ACK now (quickack mode, quickack budget 7)
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
